# Line-ending policy for the whole repository.
#
# Store every text file with LF in git and normalise on commit, so the tree is
# identical whether checked out by Windows git (core.autocrlf=input), WSL git
# (autocrlf unset) or native Linux. This stops the same file showing as
# "modified" in one environment and clean in another.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must be LF even on Windows checkouts, or they break under bash.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never apply text or line-ending conversion.
*.bin binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
